  "description": "T1 - Turkey Oak- Reduce the overall crown height by approximately 2 metres, with a lateral reduction of up to 3 metres, pruning back to suitable growth points to improve crown symmetry and maintain an appropriate form. Remove all accessible deadwood throughout the crown as part of the works.\r\rT2 - Lime Tree- Re-pollard the tree back to its established previous pollard points, maintaining the existing management regime and retaining the established pollard framework. Any branches or regrowth encroaching on the adjacent street lighting will be carefully pruned back to maintain a minimum clearance of 1 metre, where practicable, while ensuring cuts are made to suitable pruning points\r\rReason for work: General tree maintenance",
